# HealthClouda Frontend — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
# NEVER commit .env.local — it is already in .gitignore.
# Deployed values live in the Vercel dashboard under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables, set PER ENVIRONMENT.

# ── API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend base URL (no trailing slash on the host; keep the /api/v1 suffix).
#
# 🔴 ONE BUILD SERVES EXACTLY ONE BACKEND TIER. This value is baked in at build
# time, so a deployment cannot be pointed at a different API without rebuilding.
# Setting the wrong one is not a CORS error — the backend emails links built
# from its own FRONTEND_URL (staff and patient invites, org landing pages,
# cross-org consent approve/deny). If the tiers cross, a patient clicks their
# invite, lands on the wrong frontend, which calls the wrong API, and the token
# does not exist there. It presents as "the invite is broken".
#
#   local dev:  http://localhost:8000/api/v1
#   develop  →  dev.healthclouda.com   →  https://api-dev.healthclouda.com/api/v1
#   staging  →  beta.healthclouda.com  →  https://api-beta.healthclouda.com/api/v1
#   main     →  healthclouda.com       →  (unset — marketing only, no API yet)
#
# There is NO fallback outside local development: if this is unset, the build
# fails loudly (src/lib/config.ts). That is deliberate — a deployed build
# silently pointing at localhost looks like "the backend is down".
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1

# ── Site URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This deployment's own public origin. Used for metadata (canonical URLs,
# OpenGraph images). Set it per environment to match the tier above.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Auth cookies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 DO NOT SET A COOKIE DOMAIN. There is deliberately no COOKIE_DOMAIN variable.
#
# A dot-prefixed parent domain (e.g. `.healthclouda.com`) shares cookies across
# EVERY subdomain, so a session cookie minted on dev.healthclouda.com would be
# sent to beta.healthclouda.com and to production. That breaks tier isolation at
# the one layer that holds the JWT — with real patient data on the other side.
#
# Cookies are host-only by default (the current behaviour): a cookie set on
# dev. is sent only to dev. Keep it that way. This is not a knob to tune.

# ── Vercel environment mapping ───────────────────────────────────
# Branch → environment mapping in the Vercel dashboard (see the tier map above):
#   Production        → main     (marketing only until a production API exists)
#   Preview (branch)  → staging  (beta / UAT — beta.healthclouda.com)
#   Preview (branch)  → develop  (dev.healthclouda.com)
